# Corp-data artifacts — real mail / LLM fixtures and validation session reports
# must never reach git (CORP_VALIDATION_FINDINGS_2026-06.md B-2). The committed
# eval corpus is re-included in digest-core/.gitignore.
.session-reports/
.fixtures/
*.snapshot.json
*-recording.json
# Match the SHAPE, not one spelling. The corp brief's own example filenames
# (`ap-snapshot.json`, `ap-recording-v1.json`) matched NEITHER pattern above —
# `*.snapshot.json` needs a dot, `*-recording.json` must end there. So the brief
# told an agent to write real mail to names one hyphen away from committable,
# while promising they were ignored. A privacy rule that depends on exact
# spelling is not a rule.
*snapshot*.json
*recording*.json
parity*.json

# Corp notebook + diagnostics bundles land in the checkout root during corp
# sessions and carry real payloads; `export-diagnostics` redacts secrets but the
# bundles are still session data. Ignored so a stray `git add -A` cannot commit
# them (they were 176M of untracked bulk one `add` away from the index).
/ActionPulseCorpNotebook/
/ActionPulse.zip
diagnostics-*/
diagnostics *-*/
diagnostics-*.tar.gz

# Scratch copies made while editing docs (e.g. REDESIGN_PLAN.md.local-backup)
*.local-backup

# Runtime state (sync cursor, dedup ledger) — retention via TTL, never commit
.state/

# ActionPulse data home (U5): digests, logs, state — regenerable runtime files
/var/
